import json
from pathlib import Path
ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1];OUT=ROOT/'artifacts/evaluation-v3';b=json.loads((OUT/'baseline-final.json').read_text());n=json.loads((OUT/'ensemble-final.json').read_text());r=json.loads((OUT/'ensemble-regression.json').read_text())
lines=['# Deployed local policy: v3','', 'V3 uses the retrained YOLO v2 for rice, pasta and broccoli, and the original YOLO for chicken with a Nutrition5k-informed presence gate. The source, confidence, minimum mask area and gate threshold were selected per class on 197 validation images. The gate is a locally trained multilabel head over frozen MobileNetV3 Small features. All training was local; no paid GPU was used.','', 'The v2 test revealed a chicken recall tradeoff, motivating this follow-up. Its 188 images and the earlier generalist pilot are therefore exploratory regression comparisons for v3. After freezing v3, a separate 83-image subset of unused publisher test images was evaluated. Exact and perceptual near-duplicate screening excluded all prior split images.','', '**Final coverage limitation:** the remaining eligible subset contains 20 rice, 21 broccoli, 26 chicken/duck-positive images and 40 other-food negatives, but no pasta positives. It cannot validate pasta recall. Three-class macro IoU below excludes pasta; pasta false positives remain reported.','', '| Food | v1 precision | v3 precision | v1 recall | v3 recall | v1 false positives | v3 false positives | v1 pixel IoU | v3 pixel IoU |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
for l in ['rice','broccoli','chicken']:
 x=b['per_class'][l];y=n['per_class'][l];lines.append(f'| {l} | {x["precision"]:.1%} | {y["precision"]:.1%} | {x["recall"]:.1%} | {y["recall"]:.1%} | {x["fp"]} | {y["fp"]} | {x["iou"]:.1%} | {y["iou"]:.1%} |')
lines += ['',f'Three-observed-class macro IoU: **{b["macro_iou_observed_classes"]:.1%} → {n["macro_iou_observed_classes"]:.1%}**. Negative-image false alarms: **{b["negative_food_false_positive_images"]}/40 → {n["negative_food_false_positive_images"]}/40**. Pasta false positives: {b["per_class"]["pasta"]["fp"]} → {n["per_class"]["pasta"]["fp"]}; pasta recall remains unmeasured on this final subset.','', '**Interpretation:** false-positive reduction is real on this sample, but it trades away some recall. Chicken pixel overlap decreased, so this is not a general chicken-segmentation accuracy win. A reviewed workflow and manual correction remain necessary. More representative chicken masks and independently labeled post-meal cafeteria plates are still needed. The chicken/duck source proxy is unchanged.','',f'CPU prediction median: {n["latency_median_seconds"]*1000:.1f} ms, p95 {n["latency_p95_seconds"]*1000:.1f} ms, excluding app contours and network. It runs two YOLO checkpoints and a compact classifier, so it is slower than v1 ({b["latency_median_seconds"]*1000:.1f} ms median).','', '## Earlier-set regression check','',f'On the previously evaluated 188-image set, v3 macro IoU is {r["macro_iou"]:.1%}; other-food false alarms are {r["negative_food_false_positive_images"]}/70. These are regression results, not another untouched test claim.','', '## Reproduction and artifacts','', '`ml/refine_gate.py` searches validation data only. `ml/prepare_final_holdout.py` records the unused image selection in `ml/final-holdout-manifest.json`. `ml/evaluate_v3.py` calls the same ensemble predictor used by the backend. `ml/promote_v3.py` copies verified component hashes into the active model folder. Restart the backend after promotion.','', 'Active components and selection are recorded in `docs/model-metadata.json`. Original v1, candidate v2, presence classifier, and v3 artifacts remain separately available. All weights remain local. Unmeasured food weight is always null/unknown.','', '```sh','.venv/bin/python ml/refine_gate.py','.venv/bin/python ml/prepare_final_holdout.py','.venv/bin/python ml/evaluate_v3.py','.venv/bin/python ml/report_v3.py','.venv/bin/python ml/promote_v3.py','```']
(ROOT/'docs/EVALUATION_V3.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n');(ROOT/'docs/evaluation-v3-summary.json').write_text(json.dumps({name:{k:v for k,v in json.loads((OUT/(name+'.json')).read_text()).items() if k!='per_image'} for name in ['baseline-final','ensemble-final','baseline-regression','ensemble-regression']},indent=2));print('V3 report written.')
